<!--
    The IEEE 39-bus system with a meshed four-terminal DC grid: complements ieee39-dc.xiidm (Ieee39DcNetwork.create, flat).

    The machines Athay, Podmore and Virmani's (IEEE PAS-98, 1979, as M. A. Pai's Energy Function Analysis gives them): H, Xd, Xq,
    X'd, X'q, Xl, T'd0 and T'q0 on 100 MVA, here on their rating - 1000 MVA, G39 10000 MVA (the rest of the eastern interconnection,
    H 500 s on 100 MVA). The data, a two-axis transient model, have no subtransient windings nor saturation: ours, X''d = X''q
    0.75 X'd, T''d0 0.03 s, T''q0 0.04 s, an armature resistance of 0.003 pu, unsaturated; G30's q axis, which the data give no
    transient winding (T'q0 0), one of 0.99 Xq and a T'q0 ten times its T''q0, all but absent. Its exciters, the data's DC1, left
    out: the simplified AVR of Ieee14DcNetwork's machines, a gain of 20 on the voltage error within +-8 pu of field voltage (a
    1 ms lag the model needs), and a PSS1A on its speed, the pipeline's default (Ks 12, Tw 9 s, T1 0.12, T2 0.06, T3 0.25, T4
    0.03 s, +-0.15 pu), not tuned for this network: without it, a fault at bus 16 leaves New England's machines swinging against
    G39 at 0.6 Hz, zeta 0.02 to 0.035; with it, zeta 0.17 (ieee39-dc-fault-b16, run 2026-11-08 over 8 s). Each machine on a
    TGOV1, ours, as KundurDcNetwork's: R 5 %, T1 0.5 s, the valve within 0 and 1 pu, T2 3 s, T3 10 s, no Dt.

    The DC grid's converters averaged as CIGRE DCS2's and Ieee14DcNetwork's, a 15 % phase reactor on their rating (R 0.003 pu), DC
    capacitors of 40 ms, a bridge inductance for their blocking: CS4, CS16 and CS26 grid-following (on their DC voltage droop or DC
    voltage, as IIDM's control mode says), CSW grid-forming (a virtual synchronous machine), its island's. The wind park WTW Dynawo's
    WT4B example (ExampleNetworks.wt4bDynawoExample) on its own 400 MVA. Each DC line one lumped pi of its 400 kV conductor: 2 L
    and C / 2 of CIGRE B4's +-200 kV per-km pole data (OHL 0.8273 mH, 0.0139 uF; cable 2.615 mH, 0.2185 uF).
-->
